# Phase 3 OCR Repair — Iteration 11 / Node 24 Validation

Date: 2026-10-26

## Runtime installation

The user-supplied `node-v24.17.0-linux-x64.tar.xz` was installed at `/opt/nvm/versions/node/v24.17.0`. A fresh login shell resolves `node` to v24.17.0 and `npm` to v11.13.0. The NVM default alias is set to `24.17.0`; Node v22.16.0 remains installed as a fallback. `/etc/profile` was backed up to `/etc/profile.before-node24-install` before updating PATH precedence.

## Iteration 11 code change

The reward-geometry fallback now has a `requireGrouped` option so the XP fallback can explicitly prefer joined adjacent-token geometry when the normal whole-row token is too long due to a nearby medal/star glyph. A new `rewardGeometryAnchorDigitsAreUsable()` check permits one extra digit only for XP geometry used to position crops. It does not permit that extra digit as an accepted XP value: the existing `rewardGeometryValueIsValid()` remains stricter, and independent crop consensus still decides the stored value.

Regression tests cover the fragmented `2` + `653>x` geometry versus the overlong `26537` whole-row read and confirm that six-digit XP is geometry-only, not a valid reward value. Ground-truth annotations, fixture expected values, and the package lockfile were not changed.

