## Dependency installation blocker

The full lockfile-pinned dependency install could not be completed in this environment. Offline install attempts fail with `ENOTCACHED` for missing lockfile packages (including `zlibjs@0.3.1` and `@vladfrangu/async_event_emitter@2.4.7`), and an online `npm ci` timed out while attempting registry access. Any partially extracted `node_modules` directory was removed; the lockfile remains unchanged.

Accordingly, the real Tesseract.js OCR acceptance script has **not** been run against this iteration. These results do not supersede earlier Windows validation and are not evidence that OCR accuracy passes.

## Release decision

**Production remains NO-GO.** The next gate is a complete dependency install from the lockfile, followed by `npm test`, `npm run test:ocr-watchdog`, and `npm run test:tesseractjs` on this Node 24 runtime. OCR accuracy must pass for the reported screenshot, four-image sequence, order/repeat checks, and all 16 annotated fixtures; native Windows Tesseract and authorized Discord smoke tests remain separate release gates.
